  "findings": [
    "The earlier v1 review had erroneous FHDR field offsets; this version uses the packed SDK structure and direct byte offsets: prefix bytes 0..3 are FHDR, alignment/header length/section/RFU are bytes 4..7, and execution is u32 at byte 30.",
    "The 968-byte quantity is the inter-record target gap [0x302038,0x302400). Record-2 trailing six erased bytes occupy [0x302032,0x302038), so there are 974 erased bytes following the 10-byte entry in the firmware CRC span. The reported 211872-byte span and CRC 0xCEB7F4F3 reproduce exactly.",
    "All four record candidates match locked source slices and report hashes. Three RAM candidates match their record-3-relative parent slices [209964,210033), [210044,210820), and [210828,210872), and the expected hashes. Initialized-RAM destination spans are a separate address space.",
    "The report and materialization remain candidate evidence only; this review does not admit inventory records. NVM entry bytes were not instruction-decoded.",
    "For child records, historical source spans are parent record-3 coordinates; the corresponding package-global spans are record-3 file start 1060 plus each relative endpoint. All three materialized child byte arrays match both parent-relative slices and corrected package-global slices."
  ],
